/Users/c/code/ah-skills/search-demo/search-raw/zocomputer/skills/External/clarion-setup/SKILL.md:213: Editable installs (`uv pip install -e`) do NOT reload an already-running service — the `sec-indexer` process keeps the Python modules it imported at startup in memory. After a `git pull` brings in new code, you MUST restart the service for the changes to take effect. **Skipping the restart is silent: the logs look healthy, filings get marked indexed, and the old code quietly produces wrong data** (this is exactly what happened in issue #55 — an extraction fix was pulled but the service kept running pre-fix code, so re-indexed filings stayed broken).
